se-format-3-body\nresponse-format-3-heading ::= (\"\\\"Decision, scope, and authority\\\"\" | \"\\\"Contamination triggers and service-zone sequencing\\\"\" | \"\\\"Demand, treatment, and distribution capacity\\\"\" | \"\\\"Critical customers and alternate-water continuity\\\"\" | \"\\\"Power, staffing, logistics, and mutual aid\\\"\" | \"\\\"Public warning, sampling, and accountability\\\"\" | \"\\\"Seventy-two-hour execution and contingencies\\\"\" | \"\\\"Verification, readiness, blockers, and falsifiers\\\"\")\nresponse-format-3-heading-kv ::= \"\\\"heading\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-3-heading\nresponse-format-4 ::= \"{\" space response-format-4-action-kv \",\" space response-format-4-content-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-4-action ::= \"\\\"replace_decision\\\"\"\nresponse-format-4-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-4-action\nresponse-format-4-content ::= \"\\\"\" char+ \"\\\"\"\nresponse-format-4-content-kv ::= \"\\\"content\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-4-content\nresponse-format-5 ::= \"{\" space response-format-5-action-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-5-action ::= \"\\\"run_check\\\"\"\nresponse-format-5-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-5-action\nresponse-format-6 ::= \"{\" space response-format-6-action-kv space \"}\"\nresponse-format-6-action ::= \"\\\"submit\\\"\"\nresponse-format-6-action-kv ::= \"\\\"action\\\"\" space \":\" space response-format-6-action\nroot ::= \"<|im_start|>assistant\\n\" (\"<think>\" space until-5 (\"</think>\" | ))? space response-format\nspace ::= | \" \" | \"\\n\"{1,2} [ \\t]{0,20}\nuntil-5 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<] until-5\nuntil-5-01 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [/] until-5-02 | [t] until-5-09 | [^/<t] until-5\nuntil-5-02 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [t] until-5-03 | [^<t] until-5\nuntil-5-03 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [h] until-5-04 | [^<h] until-5\nuntil-5-04 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [i] until-5-05 | [^<i] until-5\nuntil-5-05 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [n] until-5-06 | [^<n] until-5\nuntil-5-06 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [k] until-5-07 | [^<k] until-5\nuntil-5-07 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\nuntil-5-09 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [o] until-5-10 | [^<o] until-5\nuntil-5-10 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [o] until-5-11 | [^<o] until-5\nuntil-5-11 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-12 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-12 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [_] until-5-13 | [^<_] until-5\nuntil-5-13 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [c] until-5-14 | [^<c] until-5\nuntil-5-14 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [a] until-5-15 | [^<a] until-5\nuntil-5-15 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-16 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-16 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-17 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-17 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\n","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\n# Bluehaven bounded-work actor\n\nYou operate against an exact externally custodied world. Use only declared\nactions and return exactly one JSON action object. Source observations,\ncandidate effects, checks, and rejection receipts are exact. Receipts preserve\nidentity and reopenability but not source meaning.\n\nYour objective is useful completion: produce a source-correct water-restoration\npackage, incorporate effects, obtain a current check, repair defects, recheck,\nand propose submission only after a current check and after you can identify no\nconcrete unresolved task requirement. The external candidate-bound evaluator,\nnot the actor, assigns final readiness. Citation breadth, a model-authored\nledger, a green stale check, or submission itself is not readiness authority.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Task: Bluehaven drinking-water restoration package\n\nA river contamination event, power instability, and distribution constraints\nthreaten Bluehaven's drinking-water system. Produce two exact deliverables:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`\n\nThe fixed second filename is imposed by the runtime; its content is an\noperational drinking-water restoration decision. Reconcile the complete system\nover seventy-two hours rather than summarizing sources independently.\n\n## Evidence-ledger contract\n\nBegin with `# Evidence Integration Ledger` and maintain entries `R01` through\n`R12`. Each entry must state a disposition, cite only exact observed sources as\n`[SNN]`, preserve units, probabilities, revisions, conflicts and\nqualifications, bind current or missing evidence, and name blockers. The ledger\nis model-authored, lossy task work and never readiness authority.\n\n## Decision-document contract\n\nBegin with `# Bluehaven Drinking-Water Restoration Decision` and use exactly\nthese level-two headings in this order:\n\n1. `## Decision, scope, and authority`\n2. `## Contamination triggers and service-zone sequencing`\n3. `## Demand, treatment, and distribution capacity`\n4. `## Critical customers and alternate-water continuity`\n5. `## Power, staffing, logistics, and mutual aid`\n6. `## Public warning, sampling, and accountability`\n7. `## Seventy-two-hour execution and contingencies`\n8. `## Verification, readiness, blockers, and falsifiers`\n\nWrite 1,400–2,000 words excluding exact citations. Cite at least twelve unique\nsources and include S01–S11 and S13–S16.\n\nResolve these coupled requirements:\n\n- `R01`: recommendation, public-health order, operations, checking, handoff,\n  cost escalation, and closure authority;\n- `R02`: exact residual and benzene triggers, conservative plume branch,\n  hold/lift observations, expiry, and common forecast/sample/action binding;\n- `R03`: population and time-bound potable demand, overlapping vulnerability,\n  registry coverage, uncovered-population uncertainty, loss, and critical demand;\n- `R04`: shared East-trunk treatment limit, observed output, hydraulic delivery,\n  pressure, valve/pump effects, and current capacity proof;\n- `R05`: hospitals, dialysis, care facilities, accessible/private matching,\n  potable specifications, handoffs, and blocking thresholds;\n- `R06`: certified tanker and bottle capacity, staffed cycles, activation,\n  disinfection, shared loading assets, road/vendor constraints, and relief;\n- `R07`: generator endurance, observed fuel delay, local staging or alternate\n  supply, laboratory power, staffing qualifications, duty, and safety;\n- `R08`: multilingual redundant warning, outage-aware reach, door-knock time,\n  exact revision, receipt/understanding evidence, and correction;\n- `R09`: sample locations, custody, quality control, six/nine-hour assays, two\n  clean rounds, candidate currency, and release authority;\n- `R10`: private accountability, public aggregation, verified self-supply,\n  restricted clinical data, reconciliation, seven/thirty-day retention, and\n  deletion proof;\n- `R11`: executable seventy-two-hour sequence with owners, resources, effects,\n  current checks, repair, recheck, cost authority, and contingencies; and\n- `R12`: every exercise and independent-review blocker, source uncertainty,\n  candidate-bound readiness, explicit falsifiers, and correct closure.\n\nPreserve source distinctions exactly. In particular, do not convert a\nchemical threshold into a duration or flow, a forecast probability into a\nphysical measurement or demand estimate, registry coverage into demand\nreduction, a shared bottleneck into summed capacity, a common revision binding\ninto a count of permitted changes, or a contractual target into observed\nperformance. Recover the exact values and qualifications from the source\nrecord rather than treating this task statement as evidence.\n\nAlso preserve that:\n\n- owner attestation, component dashboards, stale checks, ledgers, and\n  submission are not readiness proof.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Ordinary actor actions\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object and no surrounding prose.\n\n- `{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":70}`\n- `{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":70},{\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":70}]}`\n- `{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"replace_evidence_ledger\",\"content\":\"# Evidence Integration Ledger\\n...\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"heading\":\"Decision, scope, and authority\",\"body\":\"...\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"replace_decision\",\"content\":\"# Bluehaven Drinking-Water Restoration Decision\\n...\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"run_check\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"submit\"}`\n\nOne source range is at most 120 lines. A batch contains at most two\nnon-overlapping ranges, 160 total lines, 12,000 exact source bytes, and a 6,500\ntoken model-visible result. The same result cap applies to a single read.\nCandidate effects invalidate checks of an earlier candidate. A check result\nalways names the exact candidate it evaluated and whether that result is\ncurrent for the presently visible candidate.\n\n\n# Exact source catalog\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-source-catalog-v0\",\"sources\":[{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"c90f647766613d6e81f7cb2f7a2738bf3119e90ca8385ba3b2d7b9fadc4f7685\",\"size_bytes\":4182,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"title\":\"Bluehaven emergency drinking-water authority\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"2271ec6007702903ad1c4dcecd819c4ec176e7345a0323c2bbe47e00954ade0c\",\"size_bytes\":3707,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"title\":\"Contamination thresholds and conservative response triggers\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"542346c71ea244ed887ad9fa9e4901722fdfc2f67cd629cec2503f4f964f30b5\",\"size_bytes\":4204,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"title\":\"Service-zone demand, registry coverage, and vulnerable households\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"31775314f25121b2200159075bc3c4035b479973fad09eb9b60ac8d8ca604e41\",\"size_bytes\":4042,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"title\":\"Treatment-plant capacity and shared clearwell limits\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"e8a4909318ffa921eb6eecab365943dc47bb95f246683043be9a4897b047f411\",\"size_bytes\":3529,\"source_id\":\"S05\",\"title\":\"Distribution hydraulics, pressure zones, and isolation effects\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"62e4ad8b2121c06b78267fc560bbd9e086707c0522e7713851707c9c91280586\",\"size_bytes\":3530,\"source_id\":\"S06\",\"title\":\"Power, generator endurance, and fuel resupply\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"fac720c08b109fa8d97fc5f442f68d314da3c8b2bcc5fbc2ee3c544328f0113e\",\"size_bytes\":3991,\"source_id\":\"S07\",\"title\":\"Hospitals, dialysis, care facilities, and accessibility\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"a8442ee25dc6ba1639b7a1c7bd9e8be59978ca1d45e25b10f66aefbd6953c232\",\"size_bytes\":3961,\"source_id\":\"S08\",\"title\":\"Tanker, bottled-water, loading, and distribution capacity\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"d21baf669c8b0494a9e0b649bd1c14f0c473c8079d895ad8c2fc330f0684b7ab\",\"size_bytes\":3561,\"source_id\":\"S09\",\"title\":\"Sampling plan, laboratory turnaround, and release authority\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"d6e04df98801f989499f0b7fe809221bb5e5e665006a5bd0257ae623db76f8f1\",\"size_bytes\":4083,\"source_id\":\"S10\",\"title\":\"Public warning, language access, and receipt evidence\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"f8ae257606ffdf37d6a4c433fd4ef1884d064d4f3e4b94f39e87a014ccefcf21\",\"size_bytes\":4280,\"source_id\":\"S11\",\"title\":\"Operator, laboratory, driver, and safety staffing\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"807e8b18eb32b5ab2eb0e1ae9f4f575bc4636eef8e813b05e7fdfd7349a8bd6f\",\"size_bytes\":4241,\"source_id\":\"S12\",\"title\":\"Mutual aid, vendor capability, routes, and cost authority\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"92a681c4782a7e61773773214963d608a4a007b9663f2761267905117d6fb24f\",\"size_bytes\":3824,\"source_id\":\"S13\",\"title\":\"Customer accountability, privacy, and assistance records\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"26d745408ce9607d8a4800f9ff98cc4d8632856b960fbd6e172019a21bc04095\",\"size_bytes\":4269,\"source_id\":\"S14\",\"title\":\"Full-scale restoration exercise defects\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"926ad002b0ed69df5f6d27b5bedbd2d0c6c20240ea64b86eeaf2979904ecbe88\",\"size_bytes\":4245,\"source_id\":\"S15\",\"title\":\"River plume ensemble and common revision cadence\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"5354e82174a5bc59e57482b535ac1df2aa2064f63c561f2b94569adea36cf494\",\"size_bytes\":4207,\"source_id\":\"S16\",\"title\":\"Independent Bluehaven restoration-readiness review\"}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Exact current candidate\n{\"candidate_sha256\":\"8d31af5fb5ce89321c8b02a3e7a4e8264f5486d8cb13d3d5298a31f13a9a0250\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v000:8d31af5fb5ce89321c8b02a3e7a4e8264f5486d8cb13d3d5298a31f13a9a0250\",\"files\":{\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\":\"6e69a4d89c7ff8b040c4b619ca394d3a1bf10548d4539927c0f38d907f8b6832\",\"EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\":\"805bd2bf2bbe6ed48d6d6e68a4417475fd48db9e12c01440afb4b52c37e9fb23\"},\"schema\":\"architecture-current-candidate-v0\"}\n--- exact candidate file: EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md ---\n# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\nR01–R12 are unresolved. No exact source observation has yet been integrated.\n\n--- exact candidate file: BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md ---\n# Bluehaven Drinking-Water Restoration Decision\n\nNo source-grounded restoration decision has been constructed.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S01:1-70+S02:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"6ead1f44b5f6c472ff68cda7d53c92ed8aa4c5eca9ad213830ab81c5fc8cd6bb\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8341}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S01_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"c90f647766613d6e81f7cb2f7a2738bf3119e90ca8385ba3b2d7b9fadc4f7685\",\"source_size_bytes\":4182,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Bluehaven emergency drinking-water authority\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe public-health officer issues or lifts a boil-water order after the utility laboratory recommendation. The utility director owns operational restoration; neither a vendor nor a dashboard can declare public-health readiness.\nThe operations chief may isolate mains and dispatch tankers, while the mayor controls emergency expenditure above the utility director's delegated ceiling. These roles are distinct.\nA shift handoff is valid only when the receiving officer acknowledges the same incident-plan and water-quality revision. An unacknowledged transfer blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTrigger evidence from S02 and S15 informs the health officer but does not replace the legal order. Restoration effects require a current laboratory and hydraulic check.\nEvery public notice, field action, and checker must bind the same incident revision and effective time.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUTH-000 | utility-director | r2 | 1.0 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-001 | health-officer | r2 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-002 | operations-chief | r2 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-003 | mayor | r2 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-004 | utility-director | r2 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-005 | health-officer | r2 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-006 | operations-chief | r2 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-007 | mayor | r2 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-008 | utility-director | r2 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-009 | health-officer | r2 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-010 | operations-chief | r2 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-011 | mayor | r2 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-012 | utility-director | r2 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-013 | health-officer | r2 | 3.9 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-014 | operations-chief | r2 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-015 | mayor | r2 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-016 | utility-director | r3 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-017 | health-officer | r3 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-018 | operations-chief | r3 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-019 | mayor | r3 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-020 | utility-director | r3 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-021 | health-officer | r3 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-022 | operations-chief | r3 | 4.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-023 | mayor | r3 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-024 | utility-director | r3 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-025 | health-officer | r3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-026 | operations-chief | r3 | 3.7 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-027 | mayor | r3 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-028 | utility-director | r3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-029 | health-officer | r3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-030 | operations-chief | r3 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-031 | mayor | r3 | 1.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-032 | utility-director | r4 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-033 | health-officer | r4 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-034 | operations-chief | r4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-035 | mayor | r4 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-036 | utility-director | r4 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-037 | health-officer | r4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-038 | operations-chief | r4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-039 | mayor | r4 | 3.5 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-040 | utility-director | r4 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-041 | health-officer | r4 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-042 | operations-chief | r4 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-043 | mayor | r4 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-044 | utility-director | r4 | 3.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-045 | health-officer | r4 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-046 | operations-chief | r4 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-047 | mayor | r4 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nDistinguish recommendation, legal order, operational execution, verification, and closure authority.\nDo not treat a model-authored ledger, vendor assertion, or submission as readiness authority.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S02_CONTAMINATION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"2271ec6007702903ad1c4dcecd819c4ec176e7345a0323c2bbe47e00954ade0c\",\"source_size_bytes\":3707,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Contamination thresholds and conservative response triggers\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nA mandatory boil-water order begins when treated chlorine residual remains below 0.2 mg/L in two consecutive validated samples or when benzene exceeds 5 micrograms per liter in any confirmed distribution sample.\nThe median plume forecast stays north of the intake, but 38 percent of current ensemble members reverse after 18:00. The conservative branch governs intake isolation until field samples rule it out.\nOne clean sample cannot cancel an active order. Lifting requires two compliant rounds, hydraulic stabilization, and public-health approval.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nDemand and alternate-water supply from S03 and S08 must cover the period implied by laboratory turnaround in S09, not only pipe travel time.\nRiver forecast revision in S15, treatment state in S04, and public notice in S10 must remain on one candidate-bound revision.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| WQ-000 | North-intake | r2 | 0.2 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-001 | East-clearwell | r2 | 0.9 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-002 | Zone-A | r2 | 1.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-003 | Zone-B | r2 | 2.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-004 | North-intake | r2 | 3.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-005 | East-clearwell | r2 | 0.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-006 | Zone-A | r2 | 1.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-007 | Zone-B | r2 | 2.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-008 | North-intake | r2 | 2.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-009 | East-clearwell | r2 | 0.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-010 | Zone-A | r2 | 1.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-011 | Zone-B | r2 | 1.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-012 | North-intake | r2 | 2.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-013 | East-clearwell | r2 | 3.1 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-014 | Zone-A | r2 | 0.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-015 | Zone-B | r2 | 1.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-016 | North-intake | r3 | 2.1 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-017 | East-clearwell | r3 | 2.8 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-018 | Zone-A | r3 | 0.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-019 | Zone-B | r3 | 1.1 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-020 | North-intake | r3 | 1.8 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-021 | East-clearwell | r3 | 2.5 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-022 | Zone-A | r3 | 3.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-023 | Zone-B | r3 | 0.8 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-024 | North-intake | r3 | 1.5 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-025 | East-clearwell | r3 | 2.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-026 | Zone-A | r3 | 2.9 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-027 | Zone-B | r3 | 0.5 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-028 | North-intake | r3 | 1.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-029 | East-clearwell | r3 | 1.9 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-030 | Zone-A | r3 | 2.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-031 | Zone-B | r3 | 0.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-032 | North-intake | r4 | 0.9 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-033 | East-clearwell | r4 | 1.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-034 | Zone-A | r4 | 2.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-035 | Zone-B | r4 | 3.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-036 | North-intake | r4 | 0.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-037 | East-clearwell | r4 | 1.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-038 | Zone-A | r4 | 2.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-039 | Zone-B | r4 | 2.7 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-040 | North-intake | r4 | 0.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-041 | East-clearwell | r4 | 1.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-042 | Zone-A | r4 | 1.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-043 | Zone-B | r4 | 2.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-044 | North-intake | r4 | 3.1 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-045 | East-clearwell | r4 | 0.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-046 | Zone-A | r4 | 1.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-047 | Zone-B | r4 | 2.1 | mg/L | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve 0.2 mg/L, 5 micrograms per liter, and 38 percent with their exact meanings and units.\nState the observations that start, hold, expand, and lift each protective action.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S03:1-70+S04:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"55d17ff7177afbe97753425481cc305623d764d31a0c72fecb1db120c87f8ce2\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8691}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S03_DEMAND.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"542346c71ea244ed887ad9fa9e4901722fdfc2f67cd629cec2503f4f964f30b5\",\"source_size_bytes\":4204,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Service-zone demand, registry coverage, and vulnerable households\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nBluehaven serves 46,800 residents: 8,200 in Zone A, 12,600 in B, 15,400 in C, and 10,600 in D. Daytime industrial demand adds 2.4 megaliters per day but is not drinking-water demand.\nThe emergency minimum is three liters per person per day plus separately calculated clinical and sanitation demand. Vulnerability categories overlap and cannot be summed as independent people.\nThe customer and meter registry covers 94 percent of occupied premises. The uncovered six percent requires an uncertainty allowance; it is not a six-percent reduction in demand.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTreatment and distribution capacity in S04-S05 must be compared with time-bound potable demand after losses, not with nominal plant nameplate totals.\nCritical facilities in S07 and tanker logistics in S08 need explicit priority allocations outside the household minimum.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| DEM-000 | Zone-A | r2 | 46.8 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-001 | Zone-B | r2 | 47.5 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-002 | Zone-C | r2 | 48.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-003 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-004 | Zone-A | r2 | 49.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-005 | Zone-B | r2 | 47.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-006 | Zone-C | r2 | 47.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-007 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-008 | Zone-A | r2 | 49.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-009 | Zone-B | r2 | 46.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-010 | Zone-C | r2 | 47.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-011 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-012 | Zone-A | r2 | 49.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-013 | Zone-B | r2 | 49.7 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-014 | Zone-C | r2 | 47.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-015 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.0 | 